.TP 5
.B \-L \fILIST\fP, \-\-loaders=\fILIST\fP
choose the loader priority order. \fILIST\fP is a comma separated
sequence of loader names. Each entry may be abbreviated by a unique prefix,
and a trailing "!" disables fallback loaders. The libpng, libjpeg, libwebp,
coregraphics, and builtin loaders accept
\fBorientation=0|1\fP (short form \fBO0\fP or \fBO1\fP, default 1).
All loaders accept \fBbackground_policy=file_first|explicit_first\fP
(short form \fBPvalue\fP) and
\fBbackground_colorspace=gamma|linear\fP (short form \fBCvalue\fP),
\fBcms_target=gamma|linear|cielab|oklab|din99d\fP
(short form \fBTvalue\fP), and \fBprefer_8bit=0|1\fP
(short form \fBV0\fP or \fBV1\fP), and
\fBcms_intent=INTENT[+INTENT][!]\fP (short form \fBRvalue\fP).
The plus sign separates the ordered intents inside one loader entry; the
inner trailing "!" disables fallback intents. When this is the final
suboption, append a second "!" to also disable fallback loaders.
All loaders accept \fBhdr_fallback_profile=linear-srgb|srgb\fP
(short form \fBFvalue\fP) for builtin HDR fallback decode and
\fBhdr_exposure=EV\fP (short form \fBXvalue\fP) for finite EV stops.
All loaders also accept \fBhdr_tonemap=none|reinhard\fP
(short form \fBHvalue\fP) for builtin HDR tone mapping.
\fBhdr_header_exposure=0|1\fP (short form \fBU0\fP or \fBU1\fP)
controls application of Radiance EXPOSURE metadata.
PNG-capable loaders accept \fBtrns_keycolor=0|1\fP
(short form \fBK0\fP or \fBK1\fP, default 1).
The libpng loader accepts \fBchrm_arithmetic=auto|double|512bit\fP
(short form \fBAvalue\fP, default auto) for its selected cHRM matrix.
Auto uses double unless normalized primary area or a required Bradford cone
has magnitude below 0.00001; equality remains double.
512bit evaluates the supported rational transform and rounds once to float32.
Double and auto do not promise correct rounding for every color.
This option does not select an ICC backend or change PNG metadata priority.
An unavailable selected 512bit implementation is a terminal loader error.
The librsvg loader accepts \fBrelative_resources=0|1\fP
(short form \fBA0\fP or \fBA1\fP) and \fBstdin_svgz=0|1\fP
(short form \fBS0\fP or \fBS1\fP). Both default to 0.
The libwebp loader accepts \fBmax_output_frames=COUNT\fP
(short form \fBMCOUNT\fP) to cap emitted animation frames.
The CoreGraphics loader accepts \fBcache_max_bytes=BYTES\fP
(short form \fBMBYTES\fP) to cap its frame replay cache; 0 disables it.
The builtin loader accepts the PAM policies
\fBpam_duplicate_keys=0|1\fP (short form \fBD0\fP or \fBD1\fP),
\fBpam_endhdr_tokens=0|1\fP (short form \fBG0\fP or \fBG1\fP), and
\fBpam_large_header=0|1\fP (short form \fBJ0\fP or \fBJ1\fP), plus the PNM
policies \fBpnm_trailing_data=0|1\fP (short form \fBN0\fP or \fBN1\fP) and
\fBpnm_truncated_ascii=0|1\fP (short form \fBY0\fP or \fBY1\fP).
The libpng, libjpeg, libwebp, libtiff, and builtin loaders accept
\fBcms_engine=none|auto|builtin|lcms2|colorsync\fP (short form \fBEvalue\fP,
default auto in img2sixel).
The builtin loader accepts \fBbmp_info40_mode=MODE\fP (short form
\fBBMODE\fP). The WIC loader accepts \fBwic:ico_minsize=SIZE\fP (short
form \fBISIZE\fP) to pick the smallest ICO frame whose edge is at least
SIZE.
.PP
Every loader suboption has an environment default. The mapping below uses
\fIscope:suboption=variable\fP. The \fBcommon\fP scope applies to every
loader that supports the suboption; a named scope applies only to that loader.
An explicit loader suboption overrides its environment default.
.nf
common:background_policy=SIXEL_BACKGROUND_POLICY
common:background_colorspace=SIXEL_LOADER_BACKGROUND_COLORSPACE
common:cms_target=SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_TARGET_COLORSPACE
common:prefer_8bit=SIXEL_LOADER_PREFER_8BIT
common:cms_intent=SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_RENDERING_INTENT
common:hdr_fallback_profile=SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_FALLBACK_PROFILE
common:hdr_exposure=SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_EXPOSURE_EV
common:hdr_tonemap=SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_TONEMAP
common:hdr_header_exposure=SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_USE_HEADER_EXPOSURE
common:osc11_query=SIXEL_LOADER_OSC11_BG_QUERY
common:osc11_timeout=SIXEL_LOADER_OSC11_BG_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS
common:thumbnail_size=SIXEL_THUMBNAILER_HINT_SIZE
common:trns_keycolor=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_USE_TRNS_KEYCOLOR
libpng:cms_engine=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_CMS_ENGINE
.br
libpng:chrm_arithmetic=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_CHRM_ARITHMETIC
libpng:orientation=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_ORIENTATION
libjpeg:cms_engine=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBJPEG_CMS_ENGINE
libjpeg:orientation=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBJPEG_ORIENTATION
libwebp:cms_engine=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBWEBP_CMS_ENGINE
libwebp:orientation=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBWEBP_ORIENTATION
libwebp:max_output_frames=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBWEBP_MAX_OUTPUT_FRAMES
coregraphics:orientation=SIXEL_LOADER_COREGRAPHICS_ORIENTATION
coregraphics:cache_max_bytes=SIXEL_LOADER_COREGRAPHICS_CACHE_MAX_BYTES
libtiff:cms_engine=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBTIFF_CMS_ENGINE
librsvg:relative_resources=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_RELATIVE_RESOURCES
librsvg:stdin_svgz=SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_STDIN_SVGZ
builtin:cms_engine=SIXEL_LOADER_BUILTIN_CMS_ENGINE
builtin:orientation=SIXEL_LOADER_BUILTIN_ORIENTATION
builtin:pam_duplicate_keys=SIXEL_LOADER_PAM_ALLOW_DUPLICATE_REQUIRED_KEYS
builtin:pam_endhdr_tokens=SIXEL_LOADER_PAM_ALLOW_ENDHDR_TRAILING_TOKENS
builtin:pam_large_header=SIXEL_LOADER_PAM_ALLOW_LARGE_HEADER
builtin:pnm_trailing_data=SIXEL_LOADER_PNM_ALLOW_TRAILING_DATA
builtin:pnm_truncated_ascii=SIXEL_LOADER_PNM_ALLOW_TRUNCATED_ASCII
builtin:bmp_info40_mode=SIXEL_LOADER_BUILTIN_BMP_INFO40_MODE
wic:ico_minsize=SIXEL_LOADER_WIC_ICO_MINSIZE
.fi
.PP
Per-loader CMS and orientation variables fall back to their corresponding
\fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP and \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP global
defaults. The environment-variable section below documents these fallback
chains and legacy names.
.br
Recognized loader names (availability depends on the build):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
libpng
.IP \(bu 2
libjpeg
.IP \(bu 2
libwebp
.IP \(bu 2
libtiff
.IP \(bu 2
librsvg
.IP \(bu 2
builtin
.IP \(bu 2
wic
.IP \(bu 2
coregraphics
.IP \(bu 2
gdk-pixbuf2
.IP \(bu 2
gd
.IP \(bu 2
quicklook
.IP \(bu 2
gnome-thumbnailer
.RE
.PP
For \fBlibrsvg\fP, SVG input is rasterized through Cairo and this loader
returns only RGB/RGBA frames. When no background color is specified and
non-opaque pixels are present, transparency is preserved in RGBA output;
otherwise the frame is emitted as RGB (including when \fB-B\fP requests
background compositing).
\fBUSE_PALETTE\fP and \fBREQCOLORS\fP are accepted for loader API
compatibility but are ignored by this backend; palette limits are applied by
the downstream quantizer.
.PP
By default, the librsvg path parses SVG bytes without assigning a base URI.
Relative external references (linked images, stylesheets, and similar assets)
are therefore not resolved.
Set \fBSIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_RELATIVE_RESOURCES=1\fP to opt in to
file-path decode for local SVG files so relative references can resolve.
.PP
For local \fB.svgz\fP paths, the loader decodes through file-path mode even
when the opt-in is unset.
For gzip-compressed SVG data coming from stdin/pipe, this backend rejects the
input by default; set \fBSIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_STDIN_SVGZ=1\fP to allow
temporary-file decode, or decompress first.
For decode-path diagnostics, set \fBSIXEL_TRACE_TOPIC=loader\fP; librsvg emits
\fBdecode_mode=data\fP, \fBdecode_mode=file\fP,
\fBdecode_mode=stdin_svgz_tempfile\fP, or
\fBdecode_mode=stdin_svgz_rejected\fP.
.PP
SVG loader comparison summary:
.nf
loader       transparency / -B              relative external refs      .svgz behavior                   palette
librsvg      keep RGBA without -B when      default disabled; opt-in    local .svgz path supported;      quantizer
             non-opaque pixels exist;       via SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_   stdin gzip opt-in via            stage
             otherwise RGB                  ALLOW_RELATIVE_RESOURCES=1
                                                                       SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_STDIN_SVGZ=1
gdk-pixbuf2  keep RGBA without -B when      backend-defined             backend-defined                  quantizer
             alpha exists; otherwise RGB                                                                      stage
coregraphics keep RGBA without -B when      backend-defined             backend-defined                  quantizer
             non-opaque pixels exist;                                                                          stage
             otherwise RGB
quicklook    keep RGBA without -B when      backend-defined             backend-defined                  quantizer
             non-opaque pixels exist;                                                                          stage
             otherwise RGB
.fi
.TP 5
.B \-# \fIENGINE\fP, \-\-cms\-engine=\fIENGINE\fP
set the default loader CMS backend for this process by exporting
\fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.br
\fIENGINE\fP accepts \fBnone\fP, \fBauto\fP, \fBbuiltin\fP,
\fBlcms2\fP, or \fBcolorsync\fP.
.br
\fBauto\fP prefers lcms2, then ColorSync (macOS), then builtin.
.TP 5
.B \-@ \fIMMV:CHARSET:PATH\fP, \-\-drcs=\fIMMV:CHARSET:PATH\fP
emit experimental DRCS-SIXEL glyph definitions to the normal output
(standard output or the path selected by \fB\-o\fP).
This option requires an argument in the form \fIMMV:CHARSET:PATH\fP.
MMV selects ISO 2022 character output (0) or Unicode mapping 1, 2, or 3
(default 2). CHARSET chooses the starting set (default 1): 1..126 for MMV=0,
1..63 for MMV=1, 1..158 for MMV=2, or 1..697 for MMV=3.
.br
PATH receives the display characters, not the glyph definitions.
Use "-" for standard output; a blank or omitted PATH suppresses character
output while still producing definitions. A named PATH is created or truncated
when the option is applied. For example, \fB\-\-drcs=2:1:-\fP defines and
displays the image, while \fB\-\-drcs=2:1:tiles.txt\fP saves the display
characters for later reuse after the definitions have been loaded.
.br
The terminal must support DRCS-SIXEL and the selected mapping; ordinary SIXEL
support alone is insufficient. The converter does not allocate disjoint
charsets for successive images or restore mapping modes afterward.
.br
This option requires a controlling \fB/dev/tty\fP reporting both character
and pixel dimensions via \fBTIOCGWINSZ\fP, even with file output.
It is incompatible with \fB\-u\fP, \fB\-n\fP and \fB-Z delta\fP.
Delta conflicts are rejected before applying DRCS settings or opening PATH.
Select \fB-Z full\fP before DRCS to disable delta.
See \fBdocs/encoder/output/drcs.md\fP for mapping modes, cell layout, and current
experimental implementation defects.
.TP 5
.B \-O, \-\-ormode
Conflicts with \fB--update-policy=delta\fP because P2=5 does not preserve omitted destination pixels.
This option enables sixel output in "ormode". ormode is a SIXEL graphics
dialect originating from the netbsd/x68k console \fIite\fP and the twitter
client \fIsayaka\fP. It decomposes palette indices into bitplanes and
represents the index by overlaying planes via repaints, with the goal of
reducing output size.
.TP 5
.B \-X \fICOLORSPACE\fP, \-\-clustering\-colorspace=\fICOLORSPACE\fP
select palette clustering color space
.br
ignored when a fixed palette option (\fB\-b\fP, \fB\-m\fP, or \fB\-e\fP)
is active
.br
\fICOLORSPACE\fP is one of them:
.br
gamma  -> keep gamma encoded pixels (default)
.br
linear -> convert to linear RGB for clustering
.br
oklab -> cluster in OKLab uniform color space
.br
cielab -> cluster in CIELAB uniform color space
.br
din99d -> cluster in DIN99d uniform color space
.br
.TP 5
.B \-W \fICOLORSPACE\fP, \-\-working\-colorspace=\fICOLORSPACE\fP
select internal working color space
.br
\fICOLORSPACE\fP is one of them:
.br
gamma  -> keep gamma encoded pixels at the selected precision (default)
.br
linear -> convert to linear RGB float32 for processing
.br
oklab -> operate in OKLab float32 for palette decisions
.br
cielab -> operate in CIELAB float32 for palette decisions
.br
din99d -> operate in DIN99d float32 for palette decisions
.br
.TP 5
.B \-U \fICOLORSPACE\fP, \-\-output\-colorspace=\fICOLORSPACE\fP
select output color space
.PP
All output spaces accept gamut=auto|clip|local-minde|edge-seeker|ray-trace
(compact G).
SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_GAMUT supplies the default; explicit tuning wins.
Auto currently selects clip and retains compatibility output.
Local-minde uses a chroma search with local clipping tolerance.
Edge-seeker uses a precomputed hue boundary table and chroma reduction.
Ray-trace uses up to four linear RGB ray intersections and Oklab corrections.
These methods map source colors and the application palette in Oklab, using the
destination gamut, before lookup and diffusion. They require
CPU float processing and an analytic or supported matrix/TRC RGB gamut;
ICC LUT destinations reject these policies. Edge-seeker also requires
normalized device endpoints and a valid single-valued boundary model.
Mapping does not enable palette snap
or limit diffusion compensation. Explicit mapping also applies after
CLI auto resolves the destination.
.PP
.br
\fICOLORSPACE\fP is one of them:
.br
gamma   -> sRGB gamma encoded output (default)
.br
linear  -> linear RGB output
.br
smpte-c -> SMPTE-C gamma encoded output
.br
display-p3 -> Display P3 output for selected CPU palette or high-color paths
.br
adobe-rgb -> Adobe RGB (1998), D65 white and power 563/256
.br
dci-p3 -> P3 primaries, DCI white and power 2.6
.br
icc[:path=FILE] -> RGB ICC endpoint (compact icc:PFILE; path=P)
.br
The omitted path comes from SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_ICC_PATH.
CLI path overrides the environment. ICC palette snap requires matrix/TRC.
.br
Adobe RGB and DCI-P3 use the same CPU float paths and destination-aware
snap controls as Display P3. Snap uses the selected definition's primaries,
white point and transfer function. High-color output still requires
inactive snap.
They are explicit output choices; auto negotiation still resolves sRGB/P3 only.
The receiver must interpret emitted RGB in the selected space.
.br
auto[:timeout_ms=N] -> negotiate with the image destination on stdout
.br
The CLI-only auto choice uses the same stdout terminal for queries and
image output. File/pipe destinations use gamma without color queries,
even when stderr is a terminal. Any outfile argument other than an exact
"-" excludes auto negotiation, including "-o file -o -".
Explicit color-space choices do not negotiate and remain honored for files.
A final auto request cannot be combined with DRCS output (-@);
this combination fails before color queries or image output.
.br
The auto suboption timeout_ms=T accepts decimal milliseconds in 1..10000,
with a default of 200 per request/reply exchange or separate control write.
Its long form is timeout_ms=N and its compact form is TN.
CLI values override SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE and
SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_AUTO_TIMEOUT_MS.
.br
Auto saves, sets and verifies the terminal policy around each synchronous
encode, then restores its exact original value. Only complete initial
silence or a valid unavailable response permits unconfirmed gamma fallback;
partial or malformed replies fail before image output. Timeout retires
further queries; restoration then uses a bounded write without verification.
.br
For ordinary palettes, Display P3 requires effective float precision;
clustering and working
coordinates accept gamma, linear, Oklab, CIELAB or DIN99d independently.
It accepts K-means, K-center, K-medoids or Heckbert (including auto selection),
any sampling policy,
lookup none/certlut/5bit/6bit/auto/vptree/delaunay/blockcull/rbc/mahalanobis/eytzinger/fhedt,
none, CPU spatial error diffusion (including auto), or positional dithering,
none or Ward merge,
cover auto/off or soft/hard, destination-aware palette snap, and RGB SIXEL output.
Omitted cover and plain auto select the supported native float path with
repair off. Byte-eligible jobs retain their byte path.
K-means accepts any binning policy; K-center accepts none, exact, hard
or auto; K-medoids and Heckbert accept none or auto.
A zero snap approach rate selects the same path as snap none.
Supported spatial methods are FS, Atkinson, JJN, Stucki, Burkes, the Sierra
variants, and LSO2. Positional a_dither, x_dither, and bluenoise are supported.
The P3 float requirement overrides an explicit byte preference.
For high-color \fB-I\fP, P3 accepts RGB input with optional separated
alpha-zero masks and ordinary RGB/HLS SIXEL output. Gamma, linear, Oklab, CIELAB and DIN99d working coordinates
retain extended values until destination conversion. Palette construction,
lookup and diffusion are bypassed. Gamma-coordinate packed alpha uses common
frame normalization before geometry and working-space conversion. Fractional
composition retains float precision; binary alpha alone does not force float.
Active snap, GPU,
OR mode, macro/DRCS-wrapped PNG snapshots and delta remain unsupported on this
high-color path and fail before output. The receiver must interpret the
resulting color definitions as Display P3.
High-color DRCS supports opaque RGB/HLS bodies without offsets or macros.
The receiver must preserve paint-time register colors and use the matching
DRCS-SIXEL color interpretation, separately from ordinary SIXEL.
High-color PNG snapshots use direct decoding to preserve colors across
register redefinitions and transparent source pixels, and carry P3 metadata.
Ordinary stable-palette snapshots retain indexed decoding.
High-color terminal macros preserve the complete SIXEL stream, including
register redefinitions. The receiver must use the matching color interpretation
when invoking the macro.
Palette input with \fB-m\fP supports the same CPU solver choices, including AUTO.
Structured palette files remain sRGB. Lookup and diffusion retain their
unrounded working coordinates; separate P3 RGB101 codes serve only output. Image mapfiles retain loader/CMS
color information through float palette construction. Omit explicit
\fB-a\fP with fixed palettes; they bypass cover.
Palette export with \fB-M\fP remains sRGB8, with out-of-gamut clipping.
.TP 5
.B \-K \fIauto[:KEY=PATH]\fP, \-\-completion\-policy=\fIauto[:KEY=PATH]\fP
select completion source and install paths.
.br
The shell-specific source sub-options are
\fBbash_path=PATH\fP (short form \fBBPATH\fP) and
\fBzsh_path=PATH\fP (short form \fBZPATH\fP).
.br
The shared source directory sub-option is
\fBdirectory=PATH\fP (short form \fBDPATH\fP). It must contain
\fBbash/img2sixel\fP and \fBzsh/_img2sixel\fP.
.br
The install and removal root sub-option is
\fBhome=PATH\fP (short form \fBHPATH\fP).
.br
CLI sub-options override the corresponding
\fIIMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_*\fP environment variables.
.TP 5
.B \-1 \fITARGET\fP, \-\-show\-completion=\fITARGET\fP
print the requested completion script to standard output.
.br
\fITARGET\fP is one of them:
.br
bash -> emit the Bash completion script
.br
zsh -> emit the Zsh completion script
.br
all -> emit both scripts separated by comment banners.
The lookup order prefers files referenced through
\fIIMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_*\fP variables, then files installed under
\fIPKGDATADIR\fP, and finally falls back to the embedded script bundled with the
binary.
.TP 5
.B \-2 \fITARGET\fP, \-\-install\-completion=\fITARGET\fP
install completion scripts into user writable directories.
.br
\fITARGET\fP is one of them:
.br
bash -> install the Bash completion script
.br
zsh -> install the Zsh completion script
.br
all -> install both scripts.
Bash 4.x and later install to
\fI$HOME/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/img2sixel\fP while Bash 3.x
prefers \fI$HOME/.bash_completion.d/img2sixel\fP (created on demand). The
installer still refreshes the modern path when it already exists so distro
packages stay current. Zsh writes
to \fI$HOME/.zfunc/_img2sixel\fP and ensures the standard \fIfpath\fP and
\fIcompinit\fP lines are present inside \fI$HOME/.zshrc\fP. Use the
\fIIMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_HOME\fP override to test the installer against a custom
root.
.TP 5
.B \-3 \fITARGET\fP, \-\-uninstall\-completion=\fITARGET\fP
remove completion scripts previously installed by
\fB\-\-install\-completion\fP.
.br
\fITARGET\fP is one of them:
.br
bash -> remove the Bash completion script
.br
zsh -> remove the Zsh completion script
.br
all -> remove both scripts.
Each removal prints the outcome yet silently skips missing files so repeated
invocations remain idempotent.
.TP 5
.B \-% \fIKEY=VALUE\fP, \-\-env=\fIKEY=VALUE\fP
set a process environment variable before conversion. This option may be
specified more than once.
.TP 5
.B \-V, \-\-version
show version and license info.
.br
The output also lists the loader backends available in the current build.
.TP 5
.B \-H, \-\-help
print help and list available loaders.


.SH "TERMINAL MACROS"
DECDMAC stores terminal input bytes, and DECINVM replays them through the
terminal parser. libsixel hex-encodes a complete SIXEL stream inside each
definition. This doubles the image payload on the initial transfer;
later invocations send only the macro ID. It does not make the terminal
run an animation independently: img2sixel still sends invocations and
controls frame delays. \fB-g\fP disables those delays.
.PP
To preload a static PNG into macro 7 and then
display it at text row 2, column 5:
.nf
img2sixel -n7 image.png
printf '\e033[2;5H\e033[7*z'
.fi
.PP
Without \fB-S\fP, a fixed ID is overwritten by successive frames on
the first pass. \fB-n\fP is not a starting offset for \fB-u\fP.
The application must manage macro IDs, receiver storage, and redefinition
after terminal state is lost. The DEC VT510 specifies IDs 0 through 63
and 6 KiB of storage; other receivers may differ. img2sixel does not
negotiate macro support or verify that a definition was stored.
.PP
A static image is defined independently of the loader's loop metadata.
For animated input, use \fB-S -n7\fP to preload only the first frame;
definitions are otherwise emitted for every first-pass frame.
.PP
Macro output cannot be combined with DRCS output. Outer DECDMAC and
DECINVM controls are written outside the SIXEL writer's multiplexer
wrapping, so ordinary SIXEL passthrough does not establish macro support.
For the wire syntax, cost model, examples, and coverage boundaries,
see docs/encoder/output/terminal-macros.md in the source distribution.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
\fIimg2sixel\fP honours the following environment variables:
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DIAG_MODE
.br
select human or code diagnostics. The default "human" omits the LSXCLI1
option-parse header. Set to "code" to emit it for scripts and tests.
The \fB\-x MODE\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DIAG_MODE_QUIET
.br
reduce option-parse stderr noise in code mode. Set to "1" to enable compact
invalid-argument text or "0" to disable it. The \fB\-x *:quiet=0|1\fP
suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_PREFIX_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the prefix disambiguation hints emitted when a value matches more
than one option. Set to "1" (the default when unset) to print the candidate
list, or "0" to silence the diagnostic. Library embedders must opt in
explicitly. The \fB\-x *:prefix_suggestions=0|1\fP suboption takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_FUZZY_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the normalized Levenshtein suggestions that recommend the closest
option names after a typo. Set to "1" (the default when unset) to print the
hint list, or "0" to disable it. Library embedders must opt in explicitly.
The \fB\-x *:fuzzy_suggestions=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_PATH_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the filesystem diagnostics that explain why a path could not be
resolved. Set to "1" to show the guidance, or "0" (the default) to suppress
it. The converter frontends keep the default disabled; library embedders must
opt in explicitly. The \fB\-x *:path_suggestions=0|1\fP suboption takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_STATUS_FORCE_COLORS
.br
force ANSI colorized diagnostics from status markup output. Set to "1" to
emit color sequences without relying on TTY detection. The
\fB\-x *:force_colors=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_CLIPBOARD_BACKEND
.br
choose \fBsystem\fP (default) for the desktop clipboard or \fBfile\fP for
the file-backed test backend. The legacy value \fBfake\fP remains accepted.
The \fB\-y/\-\-clipboard\-policy\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_CLIPBOARD_FILE_DIR
.br
choose the directory used by the file clipboard backend. The
\fB\-y file:directory=PATH\fP suboption (short form \fB:DPATH\fP) takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_TRACE_TOPIC
.br
enable topic-scoped debug traces using comma-separated tokens. The
\fB\-x *:trace_topic=LIST\fP suboption (short form \fB:TLIST\fP) takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODE_HANDOFF_TRACE_MINIMAL
.br
emit only the decision, dispatch, and stop events from the encode handoff
trace. Set to "1" to enable or "0" to disable it. The
\fB\-x *:handoff_trace=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PSD_TRACE_ONLY
.br
decode PSD or PSB input for diagnostics without generating image output.
Set to "1" to enable or "0" to disable it. The
\fB\-x *:psd_trace=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PSD_TRACE_HEADER_ONLY
.br
suppress verbose PSD trace lines while preserving the LSXPSD1 summary.
Set to "1" to enable or "0" to disable it. The
\fB\-x *:psd_header_only=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE
Set the img2sixel output color-space name, including auto.
The value is a base name without suboptions; explicit \fB-U\fP wins.
Empty or unset leaves the gamma default. This is a CLI setting, not a
library terminal-discovery policy.
.TP
.B SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_GAMUT
Default for the -U gamut=G suboption: auto (clip), clip, local-minde,
edge-seeker or ray-trace.
Explicit -U tuning overrides it.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_ICC_PATH
ICC file path for \fB-U icc\fP. Explicit \fBicc:path=FILE\fP or
\fBicc:PFILE\fP takes precedence (path=P). The profile is read once and
owned by the encoder. RGB matrix/TRC or supported bidirectional relative
LUT transforms are required. Active snap requires matrix/TRC.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DECODER_INPUT_COLORSPACE_ICC_PATH
ICC file path for \fBsixel2png -T icc\fP. Explicit path=P takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_AUTO_TIMEOUT_MS
Set the auto exchange/write deadline to a decimal integer in 1..10000
milliseconds. Empty or unset defaults to 200. The CLI suboption
\fB-Uauto:timeout_ms=N\fP (or \fB-Uauto:TN\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B IMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_BASH
.br
override the bash completion source path. When set, the completion commands
load content from the referenced file before consulting packaged defaults.
The \fB\-K auto:bash_path=PATH\fP suboption (short form \fB:BPATH\fP)
takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B IMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_ZSH
.br
override the zsh completion source path. Shares the same priority rules as the
bash override.
The \fB\-K auto:zsh_path=PATH\fP suboption (short form \fB:ZPATH\fP)
takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B IMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_DIR
.br
provide a directory that contains \fBbash/img2sixel\fP and \fBzsh/_img2sixel\fP
entries. The hybrid lookup checks this directory after the shell specific
override variables.
The \fB\-K auto:directory=PATH\fP suboption (short form \fB:DPATH\fP)
takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B IMG2SIXEL_COMPLETION_HOME
.br
fake the home directory used during completion installation and removal. This
is helpful for testing the workflow inside disposable directories.
The \fB\-K auto:home=PATH\fP suboption (short form \fB:HPATH\fP)
takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ABORT_TRACE
.br
dump abort backtraces when \fIimg2sixel\fP terminates abnormally. Set to "0" to
disable or "1" to enable tracing. Unset, empty, or invalid values preserve the
enabled default. The \fB\-x *:abort_trace=0|1\fP suboption (short form
\fB:A0|:A1\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_BGCOLOR
.br
specify background color.
.br
overrided by -B(--bgcolor) option.
.br
represented by the following syntax:
.br
#rgb
.br
#rrggbb
.br
#rrrgggbbb
.br
#rrrrggggbbbb
.br
rgb:r/g/b
.br
rgb:rr/gg/bb
.br
rgb:rrr/ggg/bbb
.br
rgb:rrrr/gggg/bbbb
.br
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_OSC11_BG_QUERY
.br
enable loader-side OSC11 background color query when no background color was
provided. Use 0 or 1. The loader suboption
\fB:osc11_query=0|1\fP (short form \fB:Q0\fP or \fB:Q1\fP) overrides this
setting. Default is off.
\fIimg2sixel\fP sets this variable to \(dq1\(dq only when it is unset.
The loader probes only when the effective alpha policy is composite. When
probing succeeds, it treats the returned background as gamma.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_OSC11_BG_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS
.br
timeout in milliseconds for the loader OSC11 background color query wait.
Use 0 through 2147483647. The loader suboption
\fB:osc11_timeout=MILLISECONDS\fP (short form \fB:Wvalue\fP) overrides this
setting. Defaults to 50. Invalid values fall back to 50.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ANIMATION_HIDE_CURSOR
.br
hide the terminal cursor with DECTCEM (\fBESC[?25l\fP) while animated frames
are emitted to a tty output. Only the exact value \(dq1\(dq enables this
behavior. Default is off. \fIimg2sixel\fP enables the policy only when this
variable is unset. The \fB\-z/\-\-terminal\-policy\fP option takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_COLORS
.br
specify number of colors to reduce the image to (default=256).
.br
overrided by -p(--colors) option.
.br
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PRECISION_POLICY
.br
precision policy: auto, 8bit or float32, as for \fB-.\fP/\fB--precision-policy\fP.
The command-line option takes precedence.
.br
For SVG decoded via \fBlibrsvg\fP, the source raster remains cairo ARGB32
(8-bit per channel); float32 improves downstream processing precision but does
not recover higher source bit depth from the loader.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DECODER_INPUT_COLORSPACE
.br
set decoded RGB interpretation: srgb, display-p3, adobe-rgb, dci-p3 or icc.
The sixel2png \fB\-T\fP option takes precedence.
Encoder-generated PNG snapshots use the profile selected by named or ICC
\fB\-U\fP and sRGB otherwise, independently of this default.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_LSO_VARIANT
.br
set the sixel2png default for the lso_undither variant to fs or light.
The decoder suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_SELECTIVE_BLUR_THRESHOLD
.br
set the sixel2png default selective-blur RGB distance threshold to a value
from 0 through 441. The decoder suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_SCAN
.br
set the default diffusion scan order to auto, serpentine, or raster.
The scan suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_SIERRA_VARIANT
.br
set the default Sierra variant to 1, 2, or 3.
The sierra variant suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PLANNER_RESIZE_PRECISION_MODE
.br
force the resize precision planner. Accepts 1 (preserve integer buffers), 2
(linear float workspace), or 3 (float32 working colorspace). Defaults follow
the precision and working-colorspace choices described under
\fB\-\.\fP/\fB\-\-precision\fP and \fB\-W\fP/\fB\-\-working\-colorspace\fP.
Overridden by \fB\-j *:resize_precision=VALUE\fP
(short form \fB:RVALUE\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_POLICY
.br
spending mode: lazy, balanced, or greedy. Suboptions are not accepted here.
Empty or unset values make img2sixel use balanced. The CLI base wins.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_GLOBAL_BUDGET
.br
Positive encoder budget or case-insensitive all.
Empty or unset selects all in the converter. The \fBglobal_budget\fP
key takes precedence over sixel_set_encoder_threads(), which overrides this variable.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_LOAD\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_LOAD_DEPTH\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_PREPARE\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_PALETTE
.br
defaults for the \fB\-=\fP keys \fBload\fP, \fBload_depth\fP,
\fBprepare\fP and \fBpalette\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_DITHER\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_ENCODE\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_PREPARE_WORKERS\fR, \fBSIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_PIN
.br
defaults for the \fB\-=\fP keys \fBdither\fP, \fBencode\fP,
\fBprepare_workers\fP and \fBpin\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ENCODER_THREADING_DECODE
.br
Default for the encoder \fBdecode\fP key when loading SIXEL input.
The parsing count shrinks to the encoder budget; lazy parses serially.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_PARALLEL_BAND_WIDTH
.br
override the band height assigned to each dither worker. Values are rounded to
a multiple of six scanlines. The \fB-d\fP suboption
\fBband_width=LINES\fP (short form \fB:BLINES\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_DEADZONE
Discard byte RGB corrections below this Euclidean distance (default 5).
Accepts nonnegative finite decimals; 0 disables. The \fB-d\fP suboption
\fBdeadzone=D\fP (compact \fBDD\fP) takes precedence.
Applies to auto and the eight fixed spatial diffusion kernels.
.TP
.B SIXEL_DITHER_PERTURB
.br
set paired FS weight perturbation, 0.0-1.0 (default 0.0).
The \fB-d\fP suboption \fBperturb=P\fP (short form \fB:UP\fP)
takes precedence. Other methods ignore the setting; auto uses it only for FS.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_PERTURB_SEED
.br
set the signed 32-bit FS position-hash seed (default 0).
The \fB-d\fP suboption \fBperturb_seed=S\fP (short form \fB:RS\fP)
takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_PARALLEL_BAND_OVERWRAP
.br
set overlap between adjacent dither bands to smooth seams. Accepts non-negative
integers. The \fB-d\fP suboption \fBband_overwrap=LINES\fP (short form
\fB:OLINES\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_STRENGTH
.br
scale bluenoise ordered dither strength when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set.
Numeric amplitude; unset selects palette-size auto (256 colors: 0.055).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_GRADIENT_FACTOR
.br
set gradient attenuation gamma when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set.
Values <= 0 disable gradient modulation.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_A_DITHER_STRENGTH
.br
override positional a_dither strength. The
\fB\-d a_dither:strength=VALUE\fP suboption (short form \fB:TVALUE\fP)
takes precedence. When unset, use palette-size auto (256 colors: 0.150).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_X_DITHER_STRENGTH
.br
override positional x_dither strength. When unset, use palette-size auto (256 colors: 0.100).
The \fB-d x_dither:strength=VALUE\fP suboption
(short form \fB:TVALUE\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_PHASE
.br
phase offset for bluenoise tiles when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set. Format is
\(dqox,oy\(dq with signed integers; defaults to 0,0.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_SEED
.br
seed used to derive a bluenoise phase when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set and
\fBSIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_PHASE\fP is unset.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_CHANNEL
.br
choose bluenoise channel mode when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set. Accepts mono
(shared) or rgb (independent) samples; defaults mono.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_BLUENOISE_SIZE
.br
bluenoise tile size when \fB\-d bluenoise\fP is set. Only 64 is embedded;
other values fall back to 64.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_SCALE_PARALLEL_MIN_BYTES
.br
delay parallel resize until the frame exceeds this byte threshold. Default 0
keeps eager threading. Overridden by \fB\-j *:scale_min_bytes=BYTES\fP
(short form \fB:BBYTES\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PARALLEL_FACTOR
.br
override the row span assigned to each resize worker. Accepts positive
integers. Overridden by \fB\-j *:parallel_factor=ROWS\fP
(short form \fB:FROWS\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_SAMPLE_PARALLEL_MIN_PIXELS
.br
defer adaptive-grid sampling fan-out until the clipped source reaches this
pixel count. Defaults to 524288. Overridden by
\fB\-j *:sample_min=PIXELS\fP (short form \fB:SPIXELS\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_COLORSPACE_PARALLEL_MIN_PIXELS
.br
defer RGBFLOAT32 colorspace fan-out until the frame reaches this pixel
count. Defaults to 65537 pixels to avoid eager splitting on small images.
Overridden by \fB\-j *:colorspace_min=PIXELS\fP
(short form \fB:CPIXELS\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PARALLEL_SKEW
.br
bias parallel decode spans by +/-20%% so trailing workers take a larger share.
Defaults to 0 (balanced). Overridden by
\fBsixel2png \-j *:parallel_skew=VALUE\fP
(short form \fB:KVALUE\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_SIMD_LEVEL
.br
force SIMD selection. Accepts auto, none/scalar, sse2, avx, or neon.
Overridden by the \fB\-j\fP runtime policy base.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_THUMBNAILER_HINT_SIZE
.br
adjust the thumbnail target size used by loader helpers. Accepts positive
integers. The loader suboption \fB:thumbnail_size=PIXELS\fP (short form
\fB:Zvalue\fP) overrides both this setting and resize-derived hints. Defaults
to the built-in hint.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_PRIORITY_LIST
.br
override the default loader priority. Accepts the same comma separated
names recognised by \fB-L\fP/\fB--loaders\fP, including prefix matches and
the trailing "!" suffix. The environment setting is ignored when the
command-line option is present.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_BACKGROUND_COLORSPACE
.br
set how loader background colors are interpreted during alpha composition.
accepts "gamma" (default) or "linear".
ignored when OSC11 query supplies the background color.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_BACKGROUND_POLICY
.br
choose background priority for builtin PNG/APNG/GIF composition.
"file_first" (default) prefers file background over \fB-B\fP,
\fBSIXEL_BGCOLOR\fP, or OSC 11.
"explicit_first" gives those external sources priority over file background.
Invalid or empty values fall back to "file_first".
The \fB-N\fP/\fB--background-policy\fP option takes precedence unless an explicit
loader \fBbackground_policy\fP suboption is present.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ALPHA_POLICY
.br
control source alpha and omitted SIXEL pixel handling.
The values and semantics are identical to \fB-A\fP/\fB--alpha-policy\fP.
The default is "auto".
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_POLICY
.br
Set the default update policy: full, delta or progressive, without suboptions.
Invalid values keep full. Overridden by \fB-Z\fP/\fB--update-policy\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_PROGRESSIVE
Set delta:progressive (1|0, default 0). Does not enable delta.
An explicit progressive suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_PROGRESSIVE_STOP_THRESHOLD
Set progressive/delta:stop_threshold (auto or 0..1e154, default auto).
An explicit suffix overrides the environment. This setting does not enable repair.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_PROGRESSIVE_MAX_PASSES
Set progressive/delta:max_passes (0..4294967295, default 0).
Includes the initial image; 0 disables the pass cap.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_PROGRESSIVE_MAX_SECONDS
Set progressive/delta:max_seconds (nonnegative finite seconds, default 5).
Elapsed time starts after the initial image; 0 disables the time cap.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_THRESHOLD
.br
Set delta:threshold (0..255, default 0). Invalid values keep 0.
Does not enable delta. An explicit threshold suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_RESIDUAL
Set delta:residual (0|1, default 0). Does not enable delta.
Invalid values keep defaults; explicit suboptions take precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_THRESHOLD_METRIC
Set delta:threshold_metric (auto|max|rgb241, default auto). Does not enable delta.
Invalid values keep defaults; explicit suboptions take precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_RESIDUAL_THRESHOLD
Set delta:residual_threshold (0..255, default 1.5). Does not enable delta.
Invalid values keep defaults; explicit suboptions take precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_RESIDUAL_KEEP_THRESHOLD
Set delta:residual_keep_threshold (0..255, default 0). Does not enable delta.
Invalid values keep defaults; explicit suboptions take precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_RESIDUAL_FRAMES
Set delta:residual_frames (1..255, default 3). Does not enable delta.
Invalid values keep defaults; explicit suboptions take precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_UPDATE_DELTA_ERROR
.br
Set delta:error (diffuse or skip, default diffuse). Invalid values keep diffuse.
Does not enable delta. An explicit error suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION
.br
set the default EXIF orientation handling for libjpeg/libpng/libwebp/
builtin loaders. Accepts only "0" or "1" and defaults to "1".
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBJPEG_ORIENTATION
.br
override EXIF orientation handling for the libjpeg loader.
Accepts only "0" or "1".
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_ORIENTATION
.br
override EXIF orientation handling for the libpng loader.
Accepts only "0" or "1".
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBWEBP_ORIENTATION
.br
override EXIF orientation handling for the libwebp loader.
Accepts only "0" or "1".
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_BUILTIN_ORIENTATION
.br
override EXIF orientation handling for the builtin loader.
Accepts only "0" or "1".
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_COREGRAPHICS_ORIENTATION
.br
override orientation handling for the CoreGraphics loader.
Accepts only "0" or "1".
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_ORIENTATION\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_COREGRAPHICS_CACHE_MAX_BYTES
.br
set the CoreGraphics frame replay cache cap in bytes. The default is
67108864 bytes; 0 disables the cache. Override with
\fB-Lcoregraphics:cache_max_bytes=BYTES\fP or its short form
\fB-Lcoregraphics:MBYTES\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_ANIMATION_START_FRAME_NO
.br
set the animation start frame index for supported animation loaders.
0 or positive values select absolute indexes from the first frame.
negative values count from the end; \-1 selects the last frame.
out-of-range indexes fail with an error.
the index is applied only on the first playback loop, and later loops
decode from frame 0.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_RELATIVE_RESOURCES
.br
allow librsvg file-path decode so local relative resources can resolve.
Accepts only "0" or "1"; "1" enables file-path decode.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBRSVG_ALLOW_STDIN_SVGZ
.br
allow librsvg to spool gzip-compressed SVG input from stdin to a temporary
file. Accepts only "0" or "1"; "1" enables spooling.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_FALLBACK_PROFILE
.br
set the builtin HDR source profile when GAMMA and PRIMARIES metadata are
missing or unusable. Accepts "linear-srgb" (default) or "srgb".
Header-derived metadata takes precedence. Override with
\fB-Lloader:hdr_fallback_profile=PROFILE\fP or short form
\fB-Lloader:FPROFILE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_EXPOSURE_EV
.br
apply a finite number of EV stops before quantizing builtin HDR input.
Positive values brighten and negative values darken; the default is zero.
Override with \fB-Lloader:hdr_exposure=EV\fP or short form
\fB-Lloader:Xvalue\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_TONEMAP
.br
select builtin HDR tone mapping. Accepts "none" (default) or "reinhard".
Override with \fB-Lloader:hdr_tonemap=MODE\fP or short form
\fB-Lloader:Hvalue\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_HDR_USE_HEADER_EXPOSURE
.br
control whether builtin HDR decode applies Radiance EXPOSURE metadata.
Accepts only "0" or "1"; unset, empty, or invalid uses the default "1".
Override with \fB-Lloader:hdr_header_exposure=0|1\fP or short form
\fB-Lloader:U0\fP or \fB-Lloader:U1\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE
.br
select the default loader CMS backend. Accepts "none", "auto", "builtin",
"lcms2", or "colorsync".
The img2sixel default is "auto", which prefers lcms2, then ColorSync
(macOS), then builtin. Use "none" for legacy unmanaged interpretation.
overrided by \fB-#\fP/\fB--cms\-engine\fP option.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_BUILTIN_CMS_ENGINE
.br
override the builtin loader CMS backend.
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_CMS_ENGINE
.br
override the libpng loader CMS backend.
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBPNG_CHRM_ARITHMETIC
.br
select libpng cHRM matrix arithmetic: auto, double, or 512bit.
Unset, empty, or invalid values retain auto.
An explicit libpng:chrm_arithmetic suboption overrides this default.
This setting does not change ICC engines, metadata selection, or other loaders.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBJPEG_CMS_ENGINE
.br
override the libjpeg loader CMS backend.
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBWEBP_CMS_ENGINE
.br
override the libwebp loader CMS backend.
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_LIBTIFF_CMS_ENGINE
.br
override the libtiff loader CMS backend.
overrides \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_ENGINE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_RENDERING_INTENT
.br
set the loader CMS rendering-intent fallback order. Accepts comma-separated
values from "perceptual",
"relative" ("relative_colorimetric"), "saturation", and "absolute"
("absolute_colorimetric"). Append "!" to disable default fallback intents.
Override with \fB-Lloader:cms_intent=INTENT[+INTENT][!]\fP or short form
\fB-Lloader:Rvalue\fP. When cms_intent is the final suboption, append a
second "!" to also disable fallback loaders.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_COLORSYNC_NATIVE_GAMMA
.br
set to 1 to preserve original pure-gamma curve tag payloads during native
ColorSync input conversion to linear RGB. Default 0 keeps the equivalent
para3 workaround enabled. Unset and empty values use 0; only exact 0 and 1
are accepted. Invalid nonempty values fail this CMS conversion before
publishing changed source pixels; existing loader fallback policy remains.
The separate identity-blue sample/matrix permutation remains active and
moves original TRC payloads with their XYZ columns and sample bits.
This environment-only compatibility setting has no dedicated CLI flag or
loader suboption. The existing \fB--env NAME=VALUE\fP form is also supported.
The value is read at each ColorSync source preparation, not at profile open.
Other CMS engines and linear-to-P3 output conversion are unaffected.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_CMS_TARGET_COLORSPACE
.br
set the loader CMS output colorspace. Accepts "gamma", "linear", "cielab",
"oklab", or "din99d". The default is "linear". Override with
\fB-Lloader:cms_target=SPACE\fP or short form \fB-Lloader:TSPACE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_PREFER_8BIT
.br
select 8-bit loader CMS output. Accepts only 0 or 1; default 0. Override with
\fB-Lloader:prefer_8bit=0|1\fP or short form \fB-Lloader:V0|V1\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_CMS_RENDERING_INTENT
.br
legacy alias for \fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_RENDERING_INTENT\fP. Used only when
\fBSIXEL_LOADER_CMS_RENDERING_INTENT\fP is unset.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOADER_WIC_ICO_MINSIZE
.br
default minimum edge used by \fBwic:ico_minsize\fP when no suboption is
provided. Positive integers are accepted.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LODER_WIC_ICO_MINSIZE
.br
legacy alias for \fBSIXEL_LOADER_WIC_ICO_MINSIZE\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SAMPLE_TARGET
.br
request a specific sample count for palette estimation. Positive integers
override automatic sizing. The \fB-Q :sample_target\fP suboption takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_SAMPLING_POLICY
.br
select pixels used for palette construction. Accepts auto, full-frame, or
adaptive-grid. The \fB\-4/\-\-sampling\-policy\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_BINNING_POLICY
.br
select how sampled colors become weighted quantizer input. Accepts auto,
none, exact, hard, or soft. The \fB\-5/\-\-binning\-policy\fP option takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_FINAL_MERGE
.br
select the final palette merge: auto, none, or ward.
The \fB-F\fP or \fB--merge-policy\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_OVERSPLIT_FACTOR
.br
scale the provisional palette before the final merge (1.0-3.0,
default 1.81).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_FINAL_MERGE_ADDITIONAL_LLOYD_ITER_COUNT
.br
run Lloyd refinement after the final merge stage. Accepts 0-30.
Defaults to 3 iterations.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_COVER
.br
select palette coverage anchoring: auto, off, corners, faces, edges, or all.
The \fB-a\fP or \fB--cover-policy\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_COVER_GROW
.br
allow coverage anchors to exceed the requested palette size. Accepts only
0 or 1; the default 0 keeps the requested size fixed.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_COVER_MODE
.br
choose soft image-extent anchors or hard RGB-lattice anchors.
Accepts soft or hard.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_HECKBERT_CUT
.br
Heckbert cut: sse (default) or median. The cut suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_HECKBERT_ORDER
.br
Heckbert box order: sse (default) or population. Order takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_HECKBERT_WEIGHTS
.br
Heckbert native ratios: auto (default) or positive finite L/A/B.
The weights suboption takes precedence; common multipliers cancel.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_HECKBERT_PROFILE
.br
select the Heckbert preset: compat, speed, or quality.
The heckbert profile suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_ITER_COUNT_MAX
.br
cap the primary k-means Lloyd refinement (1-100, default 20).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_THRESHOLD
.br
delta threshold for k-means refinement (0.0-0.5, default 0.125).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_INITTYPE
.br
choose k-means seed selection: auto, pca, or none (default auto).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_BINBITS
.br
k-means histogram bits per channel (4-8, default 6).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_MAPPING
.br
k-means histogram mapping space: uniform or srgb (default uniform).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_SOFTDIST
.br
k-means soft-binning kernel. Currently supports trilinear.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_FEEDBACK
.br
k-means residual histogram feedback switch: 0 or 1 (default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_BACKEND
Select the k-means iteration backend: cpu (default) or gpu.
Overridden by -Q kmeans:backend=NAME. GPU execution additionally requires
--gpu-policy=auto (CPU fallback) or force (error if unsupported).
.TP
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_PRUNE
.br
k-means pruning policy: auto, none, hamerly, elkan, or yinyang. Default auto
maps to hamerly.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_SEED
.br
default uint32 random seed for k-means randomized paths (0-4294967295).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_RESTARTS
.br
k-means restart count (1-32, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_ITER
.br
force k-means Lloyd iteration cap (1-100). Takes precedence over
\fBSIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_ITER_COUNT_MAX\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_MINITER
.br
set the k-means minimum Lloyd iteration floor (0 or 1-100, default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_POLISH_ITER
.br
add post-pass k-means Lloyd refinements (0 or 1-16, default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_FEEDBACK_SLOTS
.br
number of weak clusters relocated per feedback step (1-16, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEANS_FEEDBACK_INTERVAL
.br
feedback cadence in Lloyd iterations (1-64, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_ALGO
.br
default k-medoids solver when \fB-Q medoids\fP omits \fB:algo\fP. Accepts
auto, pam, sample, random, or bandit.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_SEED
.br
default random seed for k-medoids randomized solvers (0-4294967295).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_ITER
.br
override PAM iteration cap (1-64).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_SAMPLE
.br
override k-medoids sample count (0 or 64-1048576).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_POINT_BUDGET
.br
override medoids candidate point cap (64-16384). When
\fBSIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_SAMPLE\fP is also set, the solver uses
min(sample, point_budget).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_HISTBITS
.br
histogram bits per channel for medoids preprocessing (3-6, default 5).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_RARE_KEEP
.br
reserve low-frequency histogram bins before mass pruning (0-1024, default 64).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_PRUNE_MASS
.br
retain cumulative histogram mass before medoids solving (0.900-1.000,
default 0.995).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_AUCTION
.br
enable capacity-aware auction reassignment in medoids (0 or 1, default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_AUCTION_SHORTLIST
.br
set auction shortlist width per point in medoids (2-8, default 4).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_CLARA_TRIALS
.br
override CLARA trial count (1-32).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_CLARA_SAMPLE
.br
override CLARA sample size (0 or 64-1048576).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_CLARANS_LOCAL
.br
override CLARANS local search count (1-32).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_CLARANS_NEIGHBORS
.br
override CLARANS neighbor budget (0 or 1-5000000).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_BANDIT_ITER
.br
override BanditPAM iteration cap (1-64).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_BANDIT_CANDIDATES
.br
override BanditPAM candidate budget (8-4096).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KMEDOIDS_BANDIT_BATCH
.br
override BanditPAM mini-batch size (8-4096).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_ALGO
.br
default k-center strategy when \fB-Q center\fP omits \fB:algo\fP. Accepts
auto, fft, swap, or hybrid.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_PROFILE
.br
default k-center preset when \fB-Q center\fP omits \fB:profile\fP. Accepts
legacy, speed, balance, or quality.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SEED
.br
default random seed for k-center stochastic solvers (0-4294967295).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_AUTO_POLICY
.br
default k-center auto algorithm policy. Accepts legacy or adaptive.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_AUTO_FFT_THRESHOLD
.br
adaptive auto split threshold for selecting fft vs hybrid (256-65536,
default 2048).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SPACE_POLICY
.br
bias adaptive auto decisions for perceptual working spaces. Accepts
legacy or perceptual.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_CANDIDATE_POLICY
.br
default candidate collector for k-center preprocessing. Accepts legacy or
hybrid.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_RESTARTS
.br
k-center restart count (1-32, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_INIT_SEEDS
.br
number of initial-center trials per restart in k-center (1-8, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_ITER
.br
k-center swap iteration cap (1-64, default 16).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_HISTBITS
.br
histogram bits per channel for center preprocessing (3-6, default 5).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_POINT_BUDGET
.br
override k-center candidate point cap (0 or 64-16384). A value of 0 keeps the
internal automatic budget.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_RARE_KEEP
.br
preserve low-frequency bins after k-center mass pruning (0 or 1-2048,
default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_PRUNE_MASS
.br
retain cumulative histogram mass before k-center solving (0.900-1.000,
default 0.995).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_BUDGET_POLICY
.br
choose auto budget policy for k-center candidate selection. Accepts legacy
or adaptive.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_BUDGET_SCALE
.br
scale auto-selected k-center point budget (0.25-4.00, default 1.0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SWAP_TOPK
.br
evaluate up to this many farthest-point swap candidates per iteration in
k-center (1-16, default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SWAP_UPDATE
.br
choose k-center swap update path. Accepts full or incremental.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SWAP_PATIENCE
.br
stop k-center swap loop after N non-improving iterations (0 or 1-8, default
0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_KCENTER_SWAP_MIN_GAIN
.br
minimum radius gain required to accept a k-center swap (0.0-8.0, default
0.0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_CHANNEL_FACTOR_L
.br
emphasise L* weight in Lab-family distances before snapping (0.0-1.0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_MERGE_CHANNEL_FACTOR_L
.br
emphasise L* weight during final merge distances independently of snap tuning
(0.0-1.0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_CLAMP_POLICY
Default error-diffusion clamp policy: auto, soft, hard or none.
The \fB-0\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_CLAMP_THRESHOLD
Default soft headroom factor, from 1 through 16; default 1.01.
An explicit \fB-0 soft:threshold=FACTOR\fP takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SNAP_POLICY
.br
control palette snap target search. Accepts "reversible" for legacy fixed
points, "nearest"/"auto" for nearby fixed points in the working colorspace,
or "none" to disable snapping.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SNAP_TIMING_POLICY
.br
decide when snaps run: "once", "polish", "merge", "resolve", or "all".
Named wide-gamut output also accepts "sample", "seed", "iteration", "premerge",
"merge-iteration" and "apply".
Defaults to "once".
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SNAP_GRID
Destination candidate computation: "auto", "direct", "table", "cache", or "full".
"auto" selects the small contribution table.
Explicit snap suboptions override this environment default.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SNAP_APPROACH_RATE
.br
blend factor (0.0-1.0) toward the snap target; 1.0 snaps fully, lower values
ease toward the target.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PALETTE_SNAP_CHANNEL_FACTOR_L
.br
weight L* relative to a/b* when snapping in Lab-family colorspaces.
Accepts 0.0-1.0, default 0.85.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DITHER_LOOKUP_POLICY
.br
select palette lookup policy (auto, 5bit, 6bit, none, certlut,
eytzinger, fhedt, vptree, delaunay, blockcull, rbc, or mahalanobis).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_PACKING
.br
select dense LUT packing for 5bit/6bit lookup (linear, morton, or hilbert;
default linear; other policies ignore it).  The matching suboption is
\fBpacking=VALUE\fP (short form \fBPVALUE\fP).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_RESOLUTION
.br
choose FHEDT grid resolution (64, 128, or 256; default 64).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_WEIGHTS
.br
choose FHEDT channel ratios (auto or L/A/B; default auto). The weights
sub-option (for example W3/1/1 or Wauto) takes precedence.
.TP
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_REFINE
.br
enable corner refinement on FHEDT boundary cells (0 or 1; default 1).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_USE_DIST2
.br
reuse EDT distances to skip corner refinement (0 or 1; default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_USE_CACHE
.br
enable a small FHEDT lookup cache keyed by voxel coordinates (0 or 1; default
0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_SHARED
.br
share the immutable FHEDT grid by reference after building it once when the
working palette is ready (0 or 1; default 1). Palette, representation,
resolution, refinement and metric changes require a new grid. Setting 0
uses independent builds; per-thread caches are never shared.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_CERTLUT_SHARED_INSTANCE
.br
share the CERTLUT cache across threads (0 or 1; default 0) when
\fB\-\-lookup-policy\fP does not set \fIshared_instance\fP explicitly.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_5BIT_SHARED_INSTANCE
.br
share the 5bit LUT across threads without locks (0 or 1; default 1) when
\fB\-\-lookup-policy\fP does not set \fIshared_instance\fP explicitly.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_6BIT_SHARED_INSTANCE
.br
share the 6bit LUT across threads without locks (0 or 1; default 1) when
\fB\-\-lookup-policy\fP does not set \fIshared_instance\fP explicitly.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_TILE_XY
.br
set FHEDT tile width/height; adaptive defaults shrink tiles for diverse
palettes and grow them for skewed palettes.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_TILE_DEPTH
.br
set FHEDT tile depth; follows the same adaptive policy as
\fISIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_TILE_XY\fP.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_FIRST_TOUCH
.br
zero FHEDT tiles before the EDT so NUMA systems can place pages on the worker
that will consume them (0 or 1; default 0).
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_FHEDT_TILE_XY
.br
compatibility alias for \fBSIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_TILE_XY\fP with identical
behaviour and adaptive defaults.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_FHEDT_TILE_DEPTH
.br
compatibility alias for \fBSIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_TILE_DEPTH\fP with identical
behaviour and adaptive defaults.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_FHEDT_FIRST_TOUCH
.br
compatibility alias for \fBSIXEL_LOOKUP_FHEDT_FIRST_TOUCH\fP with identical
behaviour and defaults.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOG_PATH
.br
write the shared JSON timeline log when set. The
\fB\-J/\-\-log\-path\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOG_LINES
.br
enable timeline line events and log every Nth line. Unset or empty disables
line events. Legacy zero, negative, and invalid values select every line. The
\fB\-x *:log_lines=1..2147483647\fP suboption (short form \fB:NVALUE\fP)
takes precedence.


.SH Image loaders

\fIimg2sixel\fP builds an ordered chain of image-decoder components. The exact
registry is build-dependent; use \fB\-\-help\fP to print the loader names in the
current binary. Optional components can include libpng, libjpeg, libwebp,
libtiff, librsvg, WIC, CoreGraphics, gdk-pixbuf2, GD, Quick Look, and the
freedesktop GNOME thumbnailer. The \fBbuiltin\fP component is always present.

The \fB\-L\fP option puts explicit components first and, unless the complete
list ends in "!", appends the remaining default-enabled components in registry
order. A component is normally predicate-gated before decode. Only recognised
input/decode failures advance to the next component; allocation, cancellation,
argument, overflow, and other terminal failures stop the chain.

Loader output is a typed frame rather than a universal 8-bit RGBA buffer. A
backend may return indexed pixels and a palette, byte RGB/RGBA, generic RGB
float32, or a typed float32 colorspace, together with separate transparency,
animation, orientation, and profile metadata. Source depth, the selected
backend, CMS settings, and palette/alpha policy determine the concrete result.

The builtin component began from stb_image but now dispatches dedicated SIXEL,
PNM/PAM, GIF, WebP, PNG/APNG, HDR, PSD/PSB, and BMP families. JPEG uses a
modified stb-derived float path, while selected TGA, PIC, palette, and
zlib helpers remain adapted from stb_image. This in-tree ownership improves
control over precision, colorspace, palettes, and animation but also increases
the parser attack surface; builtin is not a sandbox.

See \fIdocs/loader/README.md\fP and \fIdocs/loader/builtin.md\fP in the source
distribution for the architecture, output contracts, security tradeoffs, and
implementation history.


.SH HISTORY

Former SIXEL encoders(such as \fIppmtosixel\fP) are mainly designed for dot-matrix printers.
They minimize the amount of printer-head movement distance.
But nowadays this method did not represent the best performance for displaying sixel data on terminal emulators.
Encoded SIXEL data for VT-2xx/VT-3xx terminals were found in 80's Usenet,
But the technology of how to create them seems to be lost.

\fBkmiya's sixel\fP(kmiya,2014) introduces an efficient encoding method which is re-designed for terminal emulators to
optimize the overhead of transporting SIXEL with keeping compatibility with former SIXEL terminal.
Now \fIlibsixel\fP and \fIImageMagick\fP's sixel coder follow it.

\fBAraki Ken\fP, known as the maintainer of mlterm, proposed the method for more compressed SIXEL encoding.
Now \fIlibsixel\fP adopted that method.
\fBAraki Ken\fP describes about the way to generate high quality SIXEL.

See http://mlterm.sourceforge.net/libsixel.pdf(in Japanese).


